# Data and generated output are never committed — both are reproducible from the ingest job.
# Test fixtures are inline in the test modules, so nothing here needs un-ignoring.
#
# This matters more than it looks. A single scan's output is ~11 MB, almost all of it
# base64 charts inside index.html. Committing it nightly would add a couple of gigabytes
# of history a year. GitHub Pages is published from an Actions artifact instead
# (.github/workflows/nightly.yml), which leaves no trace in git.
data/
out/
site/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
